    53	Risks: a pending question blocks the requests behind it in the serve round, as a pending load does today. Trust and declared authority (`:principals`) are now two sets, which users can confuse; the `(trusted)` command exists to show the difference.
    54	
    55	I would not use a middleware gate on the content pair, because a gate may not wait and admission is about names, not bytes. I would not build a trust fact stream in v1, add retroactive revocation, or put admission in any frontend.
    56	
