collab/1792200000000-mob-codex.stdout.log:1669:- **F1 (P1), admission only in tests.** The real REPL had no linked Python execution at all: the Python frontend only runs the bundled prelude, which can't import a linked module. So there was nothing to attach the admission to, and I had to add a small linked path first. Please review this as a deviation from "touch only what's needed":
collab/1792200000000-mob-codex.stdout.log:1674:  `yin.repl` attaches the admission to each program when it is compiled, and serves that program's links (including later re-checks) under it. So `(lang ...)` never moves it from one program to another, and other frontends are unaffected. The new test runs through the real shell with a DHT store: a module asserted only by another declared principal is refused with `:yang.python.antlr/foreign-principal :requires :L-e`. A Clojure `require` of the same name in the same shell is not refused.
