collab/1792200000000-mob-codex.stdout.log:2157:A shared registry can support sound refusal only if admission also governs **every use of cached executable values**, recursively, under the consuming execution’s pinned policy. Checking installation under Clojure’s policy cannot authorize later Python use. A global restrictive install rule could work, but would change other frontends’ permissions.
collab/1792200000000-mob-codex.stdout.log:2159:**Risks:** incomplete provenance tracking creates another bypass; direct bindings are trusted composition authority, not ownership proof.  
