collab/1792200000000-mob-codex.stdout.log:2232:**Risks:** incomplete provenance tracking creates another bypass; direct bindings are trusted composition authority, not ownership proof.  
collab/1792200000000-mob-codex.stdout.log:2246:The receiving task must discharge each dependency obligation against the installed dependency’s **exact pinned manifest address**, including cached modules and transitive installation. A matching name is insufficient. Preserve the reader’s early binding check for diagnostics and refusal before installation. Add a test bypassing that check which independently proves core discharge rejects `t(k1)` against installed/resolved `k2`, across applicable VMs. The observed behavior contradicts [section 7.4’s guarantee](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md:1804).
