  3027	The REPL `__main__` persists across submissions (ruling 18): its module
  3028	object, globals dict, builtin namespace, and import cache. `(reset)` is a
  3029	new Python process: fresh task-owned runtime state, handler stacks and
  3030	hook attachments included, while immutable verified code may be reused.
  3031	Runtime state never merges across frontend revisions, and late results
  3032	from the old process cannot mutate the new one.
  3033	
  3034	Foreign-principal imports are not claimed until D7 slice B lands with
  3035	its tests (ruling 19), verifying closure origin and store ownership
  3036	recursively through exports, re-exports, and transitive dependency
  3037	slices before any executable value is exposed. B is necessary, not
  3038	sufficient: the claim also needs authenticated publication,
  3039	dependency-pin checks, primitive and effect admission, and working
  3040	store-context transitions on all four VMs. Until B lands, a forged
  3041	`:store-of` could reach the prelude's state. Corrected float publication
  3042	rebuilds affected derivations, manifests, and dependency pins before any
  3043	cross-principal address is accepted.
